\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Geweke's Convergence Diagnostics (1992, 1999). The table reports the p-values of the tests with different tapering steps (4\%, 8\% and 15\% respectively). The test compares the means of the first 20\% and last 50\% of the posterior draws after discarding the burn-in sample. The p-values are all well above 5\% indicating a failure to reject the null hypothesis that the distributions are different at the beginning and end of the sample. \relax }}{22}{table.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
